From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] ui: the guest's Caps Lock from its LED, tested without AppKit

What: a header with no AppKit in it: whether one Caps Lock press goes to the
guest for an input event, from the Mac's Caps Lock flag and what the guest's
Caps Lock LED reported. Each LED change is the answer to a press of ours (one
per press, within 500 ms) or the guest's own; then the guest's lock is what
the LED says, and so is a LED that disagrees with our presses as the
guest's keyboard starts (a press that came before the guest listened): a
lock gone in the guest (a new session, a restart inside the VM) with the
Mac's on is put back at the next event, a lock set in the guest stays until
the Mac's flag changes. Used by omacvm-cocoa-caps-lock.patch
(which explains the why).

Why its own file: so the rules are tested without QEMU or a window
(app/runtime/Tests/keys/test-caps-lock.sh applies this patch to an empty
folder; at build time and in CI).

Upstream: upstreamable together with omacvm-cocoa-caps-lock.patch.
Test: app/runtime/Tests/keys/test-caps-lock.c.

diff --git a/ui/omacvm-capslock.h b/ui/omacvm-capslock.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ui/omacvm-capslock.h
@@ -0,0 +1,95 @@
+/*
+ * OmacVM: the guest's Caps Lock follows the Mac's (#784).
+ *
+ * No AppKit in here, so it is tested on its own
+ * (app/runtime/Tests/keys/test-caps-lock.c); ui/cocoa.m feeds it.
+ *
+ * Caps Lock is a lock in the guest: each press flips it. QEMU sent a press
+ * whenever the Mac's Caps Lock flag differed from what its own presses had
+ * left. The guest can lose its lock without a press from QEMU: a new desktop
+ * session, a restart inside the VM (QEMU keeps running), a press that came
+ * while the guest was still starting. From then on the two were the other way
+ * round until Caps Lock was pressed outside the VM.
+ *
+ * The guest shows its lock on the keyboard's Caps Lock LED (virtio-input's
+ * EV_LED, QEMU's LED notifier). Each LED change is either the answer to a
+ * press of ours (one per press, within OMACVM_CAPS_SETTLE_MS) or the guest's
+ * own, and then the guest's lock is what the LED says. So is a LED that
+ * disagrees with our presses when the keyboard starts (a press that came
+ * before the guest listened went nowhere):
+ * - the lock gone (the LED off) while the Mac's is on: one press at the next
+ *   input event puts it back;
+ * - the lock set in the guest (the LED on, by another keyboard): kept until
+ *   the Mac's flag changes, as before.
+ * A guest whose Caps Lock key does not lock (Compose, Escape, Control) never
+ * answers with its LED: one press per change of the Mac's flag, as before.
+ *
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
+ */
+#ifndef OMACVM_CAPSLOCK_H
+#define OMACVM_CAPSLOCK_H
+
+#include <stdbool.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+/* How long the guest's LED may take to answer a press of ours. */
+#define OMACVM_CAPS_SETTLE_MS 500
+
+typedef struct {
+    bool sent;          /* the guest's lock, as far as we know */
+    bool led;           /* the guest's Caps Lock LED, as last reported */
+    bool mac;           /* the Mac's flag as last seen */
+    bool keep;          /* set in the guest: no press until the Mac's flag changes */
+    int inflight;       /* presses of ours whose LED change has not come yet */
+    int64_t press_ms;   /* when the last one went out */
+} OmacVMCaps;
+
+/*
+ * QEMU's LED notifier: the guest reported its LEDs, or its keyboard started
+ * or stopped (a reset clears the LEDs: omacvm-virtio-input-leds-reset.patch).
+ * led is its Caps Lock LED now.
+ */
+static inline void omacvm_caps_led(OmacVMCaps *s, bool led, int64_t now_ms)
+{
+    if (s->inflight > 0 && now_ms - s->press_ms >= OMACVM_CAPS_SETTLE_MS) {
+        s->inflight = 0;
+    }
+    if (led != s->led) {
+        s->led = led;
+        if (s->inflight > 0) {
+            s->inflight--;
+            return;
+        }
+    } else if (s->inflight > 0 || s->sent == led) {
+        return;
+    }
+    /*
+     * The guest's own lock: a new session or a restart (off), another
+     * keyboard (on), or a press of ours that went nowhere (the guest was not
+     * listening yet) seen as the keyboard starts.
+     */
+    s->sent = led;
+    s->keep = led;
+}
+
+/* One input event: true when one Caps Lock press (down, up) goes to the guest now. */
+static inline bool omacvm_caps_step(OmacVMCaps *s, bool mac, int64_t now_ms)
+{
+    if (s->inflight > 0 && now_ms - s->press_ms >= OMACVM_CAPS_SETTLE_MS) {
+        /* No answer: a Caps Lock key that does not lock, or a guest not yet listening. */
+        s->inflight = 0;
+    }
+    if (mac != s->mac) {
+        s->mac = mac;
+        s->keep = false;
+    }
+    if (mac == s->sent || s->keep) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    s->sent = mac;
+    s->inflight++;
+    s->press_ms = now_ms;
+    return true;
+}
+
+#endif
